event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":84,"item_id":"rs_085a5c5e713ae088016aca7f9261208195b0430e236b0392c9","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating redirect strategy**\n\nI’m considering how to handle routes more effectively. It seems I can read the priority directly without needing constants for the routes. If I replace each redirect with uniqueness based on context matches, it becomes essential to ensure exact matches since they cannot be unique. I’m wondering if I should merge the whole handler or just modify the redirect function. Maybe it’s best to replace them through broad handler segment edits."}

