event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":798,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_085a5c5e713ae088016aca7f907b948195b071bb433824cc9e","object":"response","created_at":1791655824,"completed_at":1791655840,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_085a5c5e713ae088016aca7f9261208195b0430e236b0392c9","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating redirect strategy**\n\nI’m considering how to handle routes more effectively. It seems I can read the priority directly without needing constants for the routes. If I replace each redirect with uniqueness based on context matches, it becomes essential to ensure exact matches since they cannot be unique. I’m wondering if I should merge the whole handler or just modify the redirect function. Maybe it’s best to replace them through broad handler segment edits."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqyn-V1g0JRWodhXE5m2DXB6I09CcKU7rUAxtXFiqDUg4q_DG18BNNxZbVeAFTosAdSLeAD40hkhEiDfAByn2OaoM_AquQi5c4vHnbaeyqChFgYrHpRgc3uSUm9MG0IuV3l383GC0Xnj-9DZQW2qwOYyPHokuAxgPtGNJif-aqdDl4IZj-Ti1o9HUYOwLNAAKOVzD30tPtlnaxwD8TLJA9XzXP_A2LPqaRgESY-64zMrZPpKe9N8bIGxMQPsCsiOLHe6-0GEyp4wqCwp_tF3VAH6rhjd4dptVQ-fCW0XrldiRHLRola8IotGEa6exkbSCILfdHFjMu2TQvkJkZX_zrUFyNvjWdsgVyyI_DEpkNgp3kfkF7LRgib2L1-NXyaVBIfKZWA-57PhJeW-mKsRDzCb3Y3dXTpRgczbS9OwpFedtFG0nBwZwN3YCdRQfUhlYnog1INWGoSvLOJLPm72G2PTMF4L670Y9XabDZ4xqHYIsk7Ct-Rh2kLhtp_yo43cK50_6DjJMyh4_WD-LHSaY6c2WHYrxkezuKjZugZlK-H02wri6Xf6RfIondvDGZHR2wIyAqHawawdo6r1yhs0GvT9EwCBVXrogxS_7zXyvXlarbA2n8gUdHFGubyt4XLmvzPPi36b0FOThbsZYpsKoALQAmXDWUcU5vl_6XHso3sOBHoveSOmG4DWkegoF7iICh99msXuyeFgCO5hRyP0kHoW8GnNSBMjk4wBcO9cxVMJN-cteshVLfxTvZszJwGms6ciBkR3iakwb3oQMJ6Ahf8BJdcB5rM3OLeyxIJmZe4nY1yoV_qslY1WSOitSg6Sj5Qwesj4fvXDMYpY3sGBk6oTxNAHUtoCoPXcI4lWRhYWxrjnGu5WxwjuosIQ2LDrm1teSPP6W7MGQ1ok3LCAhzE3oNrVFZP4pT1k5KgdQ1i7_RhIWJmMKvyLtB_uyUwaGNA75FooBceN9bMFECIk4RKQAid5I2xvl8MvaMWhRFVw2wF7Pi-4i8LLFVs464c8zIklY23jhgSlohU7PYPbB0QDr4Xlxh5L1XKUTgTuRHBcRNAHQqV-OqZKlmeFHc1HvF5DfZHdG8kSwWN7Mr0y8BXOmrgi_H4ViEu2RXz40lKodCRHcBzAMV-Jy7zwp6zq37Y6qIsHHpHFYYhl6rhkg9D28AdkgUAHVmNcVPSO_9DcRnXHpXvpCll2VBAsbbRI-10e3OzDE6Essh0h15S3TOM5-rhR_ymloXJoc4dspRE0tSApgQk8BGUet5K-8d2Y8hp6ROub4FFcTflUWNfM7LhMA2LD6BPqxu34HTq0anMlPRoy8vrHQZ9lVEPNLXUD4MG-ZimbjrAw-NK5EVxe7K7559bXSPd4HkyZwm1NE-OJHCAwZ2C0WiafaZH2g3y65jdkJ1UDTaGkARWngxUkYQ61uY3G0pj7oyqg5wu1Pf80wQAwj8It_9eXZntKUBZgs7DSzI7s6DXV47qvqM_Tctg64urHRHd1cmtUR6ppZYKfT3yfbz7cpi_iZfJOBkWzJsrauEevBSMNSaA6cX0rtC7hxHftIjzdGKE-V-bVsV-BTybD2jQ2eq7BNWBHu3vfZ-xUOOM-OiDwwKQHrlhDuSIenHvbURT7aEPqhIhbkGXOS5UDOt6SliUYqL1OUS23PI-vREAAHiUz6IAEvwzQf4kqa8PCZW9ivNHXrACWTIAFb7BMXpmc9-UiXJAIwmqpKYD8ey4qbytxHMbVt1fyKHjk83VVXzFw84zuQNMPBY2Sp7SNDih5h0-YJN7aWg2j0vveGH2J4HCx7XkcQhODPY7Ix_65WEUFUgQaX5fYhVru1pKIHFIjK8BiRlDSb3pvlsgw8PWzO_v2nMrSrbZMa7hs50jOMN6WXP0B5vgMmb6CZINJyAi4oEII_-4ZDgnnIpcYSEDIECloMWEr2